ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTION 2.08.010, APPOINTMENT
AND TERM – REMOVAL – VACANCY, OF CHAPTER 2.08, CITY
OFFICERS
AND
EMPLOYEES
GENERALLY,
OF
TITLE
2,
ADMINISTRATION AND PERSONNEL, OF THE CODE OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE TO PROVIDE FOR THE APPOINTMENT OF THE
DIRECTOR OF THE DEVELOPMENT DEPARTMENT.”

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That Section 2.08.010, Appointment and term – Removal – Vacancy, of
Chapter 2.08, City Officers and Employees Generally, of Title 2, Administration and Personnel,
of the code of the City of Cheyenne is hereby amended as forth in this ordinance to provide for
the appointment of the director of the development department.  Sections currently existing
within Chapter 2.08 not set out within this ordinance remain unchanged.

2.08.010
Appointment and term – Removal – Vacancy.

A.  At the first regular meeting of the city council GOVERNING BODY in the official
year following the city election, OR AT SUCH OTHER TIMES AS NEEDED TO FILL AN
APPOINTED POSITION SET FORTH IN THIS SECTION, there shall be appointed by the
mayor, by and with the consent of the city council, the following officers:  city clerk, city
treasurer, city engineer, city attorney, fire chief, police chief, judge of the municipal court, judge
of the juvenile court, public works manager DIRECTOR, planning services director, parks and
recreation director, DEVELOPMENT DIRECTOR, and such other officers and employees as
are necessary for the efficient operation of the city.

B.  Each appointed officer APPOINTED PURSUANT TO SUB-SECTION 2.28.010
A., shall hold office for A the term of two (2) years or until his or her successor is appointed and
qualified.  "B.  Each officer appointed pursuant to Sub-Section 2.08.010 A., shall hold office for
a term of two (2) years, PROVIDED HOWEVER, THAT THE SPECIFIC BEGINNING
AND ENDING DATES OF THE TERM OF APPOINTMENT SHALL BE SPECIFIED IN
THE CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT.

Section 2.  That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its passage and
publication.

FIRST READING:

__________________________________

SECOND READING:

__________________________________

THIRD AND FINAL READING:
__________________________________

(S E A L)

___________________________________

RICHARD L. KAYSEN, MAYOR

ATTEST:

_________________________________
CAROL INTLEKOFER, CITY CLERK

Publish:  Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
